{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.BetaStability","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.BetaStability","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.nOverP_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.nOverP_classical","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/beta-stability.lean#L59-L67","doc":"The n/p ratio is 1 when the stable mass number is 2p (the\nsymmetric a_C = 0 fixed point). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.stableNeutronNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.stableNeutronNumber","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/beta-stability.lean#L53-L57","doc":"Stable neutron number: n*(p) = A*(p) - p where A*(p) is the\nfixed point of A = p·(2 + a_C·A^{2/3}/(2·a_A)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.neutron_excess","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.neutron_excess","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/beta-stability.lean#L40-L51","doc":"The denominator of the stability line is > 2 when a_C > 0 and A > 0,\nso p*(A) < A/2: heavy nuclei have more neutrons than protons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.classical_limit_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.classical_limit_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/beta-stability.lean#L32-L38","doc":"At a_C = 0 (no Coulomb repulsion), all nuclei have p = A/2:\nsymmetric nuclear matter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.betaStabilityLine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.betaStabilityLine","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/beta-stability.lean#L27-L30","doc":"Beta-stability line: p*(A) = A / (2 + a_C·A^{2/3}/(2·a_A)). ","signatureChunk":0}]}